<title>USA: Suffolk County, N.Y., voters support new county.</title>
<headline>Suffolk County, N.Y., voters support new county.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 75 percent of the voters who live in Suffolk County on the eastern end of Long Island supported a proposal to secede from that county and form a new one, to be called Peconic County.</p>
<p>The secessionst voters were concerned about overdevelopment and want to preserve the rural character of their area.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
